## Reagraph Contract

Reagraph provides WebGL network graph rendering for node/link datasets. Use it when the app needs an
interactive force-directed or hierarchical graph over explicit `nodes` and `edges` arrays, especially
for larger or more dynamic relationship views where plain SVG/CSS would be limiting.
## Reagraph Contract

`reagraph` is available for interactive WebGL network graphs in React.

- Import `GraphCanvas` from `reagraph` and pass `nodes` and `edges` arrays.
- Follow the minimal platform contract in `src/platform/reagraph/README.md`.
- Each node needs a stable string `id` and a display `label`. Each edge needs a stable string `id`, plus `source` and `target` node ids.
- `GraphCanvas` fills its parent element, so wrap it in a parent with explicit, stable width and height.
- Keep graph data in React state or memoized values; update `nodes`, `edges`, and interaction props declaratively.
